The  driver provides support for Fibocom L850‐GL / Intel XMM7360.
The device establishes connections via cellular networks such  as
GPRS,  UMTS,  and  LTE.   They appear as a regular point‐to‐point
network interface, transporting raw  IP  frames.   The  SIM  card
needs  to  be unlocked, the driver provides no means to provide a
password for the SIM.  The following devices should work: The de‐
vice driver first appeared Development of the  Linux  and  driver
was  supported  by  genua  GmbH.   The  driver was written by for
Linux, it was ported to and by for Moritz Systems Technology Com‐
pany Sp. z o.o.  The driver IPv6 support  is  untested.   Network
initialization  requires  a  Python script published in the Linux
driver repository, available as package The script  requires  the
management  device  nodes to be created via: cd /dev && ./MAKEDEV
